            "The protocol for boredom is the same as the protocol for panic, which tells you something: the emotion is irrelevant, the check is everything. Name it — 'this is boredom, not information'. Check the three lines — nothing has changed. Then do what the professional does in the boring middle: walk away. The position does not need supervision; it needs abandonment. The traders who die in the boring middle are not killed by the market. They are killed by their own attention, starving for stimulation, mistaking boredom for a signal."
